# Decision Template

Use when a consequential decision needs to survive a handoff. Follow the existing project decision format if present. This template is not an accepted decision.

## Question and status

State the choice, applicable revision/context, status, and date. Record who actually decided and existing authorization when known; leave an undecided choice explicit.

## Constraints and evidence

Record confirmed requirements and observations with sources. Separate legitimate preferences from unsupported assumptions. Avoid invented traffic, performance, cost, or staffing measurements.

## Options and tradeoffs

Compare credible alternatives against the same constraints, including retaining the current arrangement when relevant. Describe consumer effects, complexity/ownership costs, and recovery limits.

## Decision or next experiment

Record the actual choice and rationale, or the discriminating experiment and proposed acceptance threshold. A proposal is not approval and a planned experiment is not measured evidence. Preserve settled decisions unless new evidence changes them.

## Consequences and reconsideration

Record relevant consequences, remaining uncertainty, and observable conditions that would justify revisiting the choice. Use existing project links; do not mandate a particular architecture style or deployment model.
